<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p><h1 class="research-title">48 BCE</h1><p class="ref-lede">48 BCE in world history: 6 events, 1 birth and 1 death. 177 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/53-bce">53 BCE</a><a href="/years/52-bce">52 BCE</a><a href="/years/51-bce">51 BCE</a><a href="/years/49-bce">49 BCE</a><a href="/years/48-bce" aria-current="page">48 BCE</a><a href="/years/47-bce">47 BCE</a><a href="/years/46-bce">46 BCE</a><a href="/years/45-bce">45 BCE</a><a href="/years/44-bce">44 BCE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-9">9 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Caesar defeats Pompey at Pharsalus</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>'s veterans routed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>'s larger army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a>. Pompey fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, where he was murdered, and Caesar became master of the Roman world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pompey" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pompey.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-28">28 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pompey is murdered on landing in Egypt</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Fleeing after Pharsalus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> the Great was stabbed to death as he stepped ashore, on the orders of Ptolemy XIII's advisers. Caesar is said to have wept when shown his rival's head.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julius-caesar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-2">2 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar arrives in Egypt and learns of Pompey's death</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>, pursuing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>, arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>, capital of Ptolemaic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and learned of his rival's death. Kept there by the Etesian winds, he went on to arbitrate the civil war between the child <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> Ptolemy XIII and Cleopatra.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Kingdom</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pharsalus">Battle of Pharsalus</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Pharsalus was fought on 9 August 48 BCE near Pharsalus in Thessaly between Julius Caesar and the larger army of Pompey and the Senate.</p></div></li></ol></section>
